</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwKQ"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Career">Career</h2>
<p id="mwKg">Powell began his career at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Oberlin_College" title="Oberlin College" id="mwKw">Oberlin College</a> in 1962 where he held the position of chair of the geology department from 1965 to 1973. He became the associate dean of arts and science in 1973, then vice president and provost in 1975.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt14" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"AMWS\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwLA"/><sup about="#mwt14" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AMWS_2-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"AMWS"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-AMWS-2" id="mwLQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLw">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA">]</span></span></a></sup> After serving two years as a visiting administrator at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Stanford_University" title="Stanford University" id="mwMQ">Stanford University</a>, Powell returned to Oberlin to serve as its acting president from 1981 to 1983.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt18" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"OberlinArchive\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwMg"/><sup about="#mwt18" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-OberlinArchive_3-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"OberlinArchive"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-OberlinArchive-3" id="mwMw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNQ">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwNw">Following a 20-year career at Oberlin, Powell served as president of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Franklin_and_Marshall_College" title="Franklin and Marshall College" class="mw-redirect" id="mwOA">Franklin and Marshall College</a> from 1983 to 1988,<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt22" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"FandM\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwOQ"/><sup about="#mwt22" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FandM_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FandM"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-FandM-4" id="mwOg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwOw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPA">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPQ">]</span></span></a></sup> then president of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Reed_College" title="Reed College" id="mwPg">Reed College</a> from 1988 to 1991.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt26" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Reed\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwPw"/><sup about="#mwt26" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Reed_5-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Reed"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Reed-5" id="mwQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQw">]</span></span></a></sup> Powell left academia to preside over the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Franklin_Institute" title="Franklin Institute" id="mwRA">Franklin Institute</a> (1991–1994)<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt30" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"FranklinInstitute\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwRQ"/><sup about="#mwt30" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FranklinInstitute_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FranklinInstitute"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-FranklinInstitute-6" id="mwRg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwRw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSA">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSQ">]</span></span></a></sup> followed by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Natural_History_Museum_of_Los_Angeles_County" title="Natural History Museum of Los Angeles County" id="mwSg">National History Museum of Los Angeles</a> (1994–2001).<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt34" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"NHMLA\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwSw"/><sup about="#mwt34" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NHMLA_7-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"NHMLA"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-NHMLA-7" id="mwTA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTg">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTw">]</span></span></a></sup> Since 2001, Powell has been serving as the executive director of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./National_Physical_Science_Consortium" title="National Physical Science Consortium" id="mwUA">National Physical Science Consortium</a>.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt38" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Reed\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwUQ"/><sup about="#mwt38" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Reed_5-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Reed"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Reed-5" id="mwUg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwUw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVA">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVQ">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt42" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"PowellBio\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwVg"/><sup about="#mwt42" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-PowellBio_8-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"PowellBio"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-PowellBio-8" id="mwVw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWQ">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwWw">Powell served 12 years on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./National_Science_Board" title="National Science Board" id="mwXA">National Science Board</a> first appointed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Ronald_Reagan" title="Ronald Reagan" id="mwXQ">Ronald Reagan</a> in 1986 and serving as its vice chair in 1990.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt46" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"NSF\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwXg"/><sup about="#mwt46" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NSF_9-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"NSF"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-NSF-9" id="mwXw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwYA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYQ">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwYw"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Committee_for_Skeptical_Inquiry">Committee for Skeptical Inquiry</h2>
<p id="mwZA">In 2015, Powell was named a fellow for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Committee_for_Skeptical_Inquiry" title="Committee for Skeptical Inquiry" id="mwZQ">Committee for Skeptical Inquiry</a>.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt50" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"CSI\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwZg"/><sup about="#mwt50" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CSI_10-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"CSI"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-CSI-10" id="mwZw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwaA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaQ">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwag">]</span></span></a></sup> He resigned in March 2022 in protest against the publication of an article in <i id="mwaw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Skeptical_Inquirer" title="Skeptical Inquirer" id="mwbA">Skeptical Inquirer</a></i> by CSI fellow <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Mark_Boslough" title="Mark Boslough" id="mwbQ">Mark Boslough</a> regarding the Bunch et al. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Tall_el-Hammam#Air_burst_claim" title="Tall el-Hammam" class="mw-redirect" id="mwbg">Tall el-Hammam airburst</a> paper,<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt54" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Pillar of Salt"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwbw"/><sup about="#mwt54" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Pillar_of_Salt_11-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Pillar of Salt"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Pillar_of_Salt-11" id="mwcA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcg">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcw">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt58" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Bunch et al."}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwdA"/><sup about="#mwt58" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bunch_et_al._12-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Bunch et al."},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Bunch_et_al.-12" id="mwdQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdw">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mweA">]</span></span></a></sup>, which had been based on research funded by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Comet_Research_Group" title="Comet Research Group" class="mw-redirect" id="mweQ">Comet Research Group</a> (CRG) and authored primarily by its members. He stated that it "violates nearly every tenet of proper skepticism" as defined by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Committee_for_Skeptical_Inquiry" title="Committee for Skeptical Inquiry" id="mweg">CSICOP and CSI</a>, citing CSI-co-founder and executive council member <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Ray_Hyman" title="Ray Hyman" id="mwew">Ray Hyman</a>.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt62" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"PowellResignation\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwfA"/><sup about="#mwt62" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-PowellResignation_13-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"PowellResignation"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-PowellResignation-13" id="mwfQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfw">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwgQ">On February 15, 2023, the following editor's note was posted on the Bunch et al. paper: "Readers are alerted that concerns raised about the data presented and the conclusions of this article are being considered by the Editors. A further editorial response will follow the resolution of these issues."<sup about="#mwt68" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-14"}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-14" id="mwgg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwgw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhA">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhQ">]</span></span></a></sup> On April 24, 2025, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Nature_(journal)" title="Nature (journal)" id="mwhg">Nature</a> issued a formal <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Retraction_in_academic_publishing" title="Retraction in academic publishing" class="mw-redirect" id="mwhw">retraction note</a>, citing concerns about methodology, analysis, and data interpretation.<sup about="#mwt71" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-15"}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-15" id="mwiA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwiQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwig">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiw">]</span></span></a></sup> Also on April 24, 2025, an expanded version with the same title was submitted to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Comet_Research_Group" title="Comet Research Group" class="mw-redirect" id="mwjA">Comet Research Group</a> journal “Airbursts and Cratering Impacts”, for which Powell serves as co-editor. It was accepted for publication on May 4, 2025.<sup about="#mwt74" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-16"}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-16" id="mwjQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwjg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjw">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwkQ"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Debate_on_climate_change_consensus">Debate on climate change consensus</h2>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwkg"><a href="./File:The_Consensus_on_Anthropogenic_Global_Warming,_2017.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwkw"><img resource="./File:The_Consensus_on_Anthropogenic_Global_Warming,_2017.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/The_Consensus_on_Anthropogenic_Global_Warming%2C_2017.jpg/250px-The_Consensus_on_Anthropogenic_Global_Warming%2C_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/The_Consensus_on_Anthropogenic_Global_Warming%2C_2017.jpg/500px-The_Consensus_on_Anthropogenic_Global_Warming%2C_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3300" data-file-height="2550" data-file-type="bitmap" height="193" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwlA"/></a><figcaption id="mwlQ">Early peer-reviewed studies of the consensus on anthropogenic global warming</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwlg"><a href="./File:20211103_Academic_studies_of_scientific_consensus_-_global_warming,_climate_change_-_vertical_bar_chart_-_en.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwlw"><img resource="./File:20211103_Academic_studies_of_scientific_consensus_-_global_warming,_climate_change_-_vertical_bar_chart_-_en.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/20211103_Academic_studies_of_scientific_consensus_-_global_warming%2C_climate_change_-_vertical_bar_chart_-_en.svg/250px-20211103_Academic_studies_of_scientific_consensus_-_global_warming%2C_climate_change_-_vertical_bar_chart_-_en.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/20211103_Academic_studies_of_scientific_consensus_-_global_warming%2C_climate_change_-_vertical_bar_chart_-_en.svg/500px-20211103_Academic_studies_of_scientific_consensus_-_global_warming%2C_climate_change_-_vertical_bar_chart_-_en.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1000" data-file-height="750" data-file-type="drawing" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwmA"/></a><figcaption id="mwmQ"><i id="mwmg">Scientific consensus on causation:</i> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Surveys_of_scientists'_views_on_climate_change" title="Surveys of scientists' views on climate change" class="mw-redirect" id="mwmw">Academic studies of scientific agreement on human-caused global warming</a> among climate experts (2010–2015) reflect that the level of consensus correlates with expertise in climate science.<sup about="#mwt77" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Cook_2016_17-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Cook_2016"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Cook_2016-17"}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Cook_2016-17" id="mwnA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwnQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwng">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnw">]</span></span></a></sup> A 2019 study found scientific consensus to be at 100%,<sup about="#mwt80" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Powell2019_18-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Powell2019"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Powell2019-18"}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Powell2019-18" id="mwoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwoQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwog">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwow">]</span></span></a></sup> and a 2021 study concluded that consensus exceeded 99%. Another 2021 study found that 98.7% of climate experts indicated that the Earth is getting warmer mostly because of human activity.</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwpA">Powell has researched the scientific consensus view of anthropogenic <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Global_warming" title="Global warming" class="mw-redirect" id="mwpQ">global warming</a> (AGW) in a series of studies evaluating the peer-reviewed literature. In 2012, Powell reviewed 13,950 peer-reviewed publications between 1991 and 2012 with "global warming" or "global climate change" as keywords. Evaluating this dataset, Powell showed a 99.97% scientific consensus view supporting AGW.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt81" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Plait\""},"2":{"wt":"\"Sheppard\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwpg"/><sup about="#mwt81" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Plait_19-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Plait"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Plait-19" id="mwpw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwqA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqQ">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt81" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Sheppard_20-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Sheppard"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Sheppard-20" id="mwqw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwrA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrQ">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrg">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2016, Powell duplicated this method on articles published during 2013 and 2014. In this set, Powell found a 99.99% consensus "verging on unanimity" by the scientific community.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt87" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"BSTS1\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwrw"/><sup about="#mwt87" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BSTS1_21-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"BSTS1"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-BSTS1-21" id="mwsA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwsQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsg">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwtA">While agreeing that the consensus on AGW is high, other scientists argued <i id="mwtQ">ca</i> 2010-2013 that the consensus is closer to 97%.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt91" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Cook\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwtg"/><sup about="#mwt91" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Cook_22-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Cook"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Cook-22" id="mwtw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwuA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuQ">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwug">]</span></span></a></sup> <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt95" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"PNAS\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwuw"/><sup about="#mwt95" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-PNAS_23-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"PNAS"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-PNAS-23" id="mwvA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvg">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvw">]</span></span></a></sup> The debate centers around the selection of scientific papers identified as supporting AGW and therefore included in the study.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt99" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Skuce\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwwA"/><sup about="#mwt99" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Skuce_24-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Skuce"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Skuce-24" id="mwwQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwwg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwww">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxA">]</span></span></a></sup> For example, in their 2013 study, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Quantifying_the_consensus_on_anthropogenic_global_warming_in_the_scientific_literature" title="Quantifying the consensus on anthropogenic global warming in the scientific literature" class="mw-redirect" id="mwxQ">Cook et al.</a> excluded 66.4% of the papers examined because the abstracts did not endorse AGW either explicitly or implicitly.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt103" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Cook\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwxg"/><sup about="#mwt103" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Cook_22-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Cook"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Cook-22" id="mwxw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwyA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyQ">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyg">]</span></span></a></sup> Powell reviewed the abstracts of hundreds of articles on plate tectonics, evolution, and impact cratering to show that scientists almost never directly affirm the ruling paradigm of their discipline. On that basis, Powell included papers in the study as long as the abstracts did not explicitly reject AGW.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt107" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"BSTS1\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwyw"/><sup about="#mwt107" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BSTS1_21-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"BSTS1"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-BSTS1-21" id="mwzA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwzQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzg">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw0A">Powell has further argued that the extent of the scientific consensus is important. In <i id="mw0Q">The Consensus on Anthropogenic Warming Matters</i> Powell argues that the "stronger the public believe the consensus to be, the more they support the action on global warming that human society so desperately needs." This metastudy included 54,195 publications from five earlier studies by Powell and others demonstrating that the scientific consensus on AGW is 99.94%.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt111" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"BSTS2\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mw0g"/><sup about="#mwt111" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BSTS2_25-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"BSTS2"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-BSTS2-25" id="mw0w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw1A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1Q">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw1w">In November 2019, Powell published "Scientists Reach 100% Consensus on Anthropogenic Global Warming."<sup about="#mwt117" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-26" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-26"}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-26" id="mw2A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw2Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2g">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2w">]</span></span></a></sup> He reviewed over 11,600 peer-reviewed articles published in the first seven months of 2019 but found none that rejected anthropogenic global warming.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mw3A"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Views_and_scientific_activism">Views and scientific activism</h2>
<p id="mw3Q">Powell has encouraged scientists to do more than publish in scientific journals. "I think it's time for scientists to get up from the lab bench and speak out." Concerning the consequences of global warming, Powell said: "I want my grandchildren to be able to say... he did something. He tried to do something."<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt118" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"BigThink\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mw3g"/><sup about="#mwt118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BigThink_27-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"BigThink"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-BigThink-27" id="mw3w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw4A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4Q">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw4w">There is no scientific debate regarding the existence of AGW according to Powell. Through his research and other publications Powell has criticized politicians and others who defy the scientific consensus by denying AGW. <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt122" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"BigThink\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mw5A"/><sup about="#mwt122" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BigThink_27-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"BigThink"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-BigThink-27" id="mw5Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw5g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5w">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6A">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt126" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"BSTS1\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mw6Q"/><sup about="#mwt126" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BSTS1_21-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"BSTS1"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-BSTS1-21" id="mw6g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw6w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7A">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7Q">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt130" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Salon\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mw7g"/><sup about="#mwt130" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Salon_28-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Salon"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Salon-28" id="mw7w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw8A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8Q">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw8w">In a 2014 editorial, Powell urged the university presidents of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Brown_University" title="Brown University" id="mw9A">Brown University</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Harvard_University" title="Harvard University" id="mw9Q">Harvard University</a> to change course by divesting their institutions from fossil fuels.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt134" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Harvard\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mw9g"/><sup about="#mwt134" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Harvard_29-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Harvard"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Harvard-29" id="mw9w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw-A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-Q">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-g">]</span></span></a></sup> A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./The_New_York_Times" title="The New York Times" id="mw-w">New York Times</a> editorial co-authored by Powell and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Michael_E._Mann" title="Michael E. Mann" id="mw_A">Michael E. Mann</a> recommended that the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./American_Museum_of_Natural_History" title="American Museum of Natural History" id="mw_Q">American Museum of Natural History</a> remove <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Rebekah_Mercer" title="Rebekah Mercer" id="mw_g">Rebekah Mercer</a> from their board as her family foundation supported <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Climate_change_denialism" title="Climate change denialism" class="mw-redirect" id="mw_w">climate change denialism</a>.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt138" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Mercer\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwAQA"/><sup about="#mwt138" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Mercer_30-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Mercer"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Mercer-30" id="mwAQE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQM">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAQU">In a self-published 2020 book,<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt142" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"DeadlyVoyager\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwAQY"/><sup about="#mwt142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-DeadlyVoyager_31-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"DeadlyVoyager"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-DeadlyVoyager-31" id="mwAQc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQk">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQo">]</span></span></a></sup> Powell defended the controversial <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Younger_Dryas_impact_hypothesis" title="Younger Dryas impact hypothesis" id="mwAQs">Younger Dryas impact hypothesis</a> which has been rejected by the mainstream scientific community. In 2022 he published a paper in the journal <i id="mwAQw">Scientific Progress</i>, writing that this scientific rejection was premature.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt146" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"Rejection\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwAQ0"/><sup about="#mwt146" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Rejection_32-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"Rejection"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-Rejection-32" id="mwAQ4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQ8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARA">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARE">]</span></span></a></sup> His concerns have been critiqued in a comprehensive review of the literature on this subject.<sup about="#mwt152" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_33-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-33"}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-:1-33" id="mwARI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARQ">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwARY"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Recognition">Recognition</h2>
<p id="mwARc">Powell is the recipient of several honorary degrees. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Oberlin_College" title="Oberlin College" id="mwARg">Oberlin College</a> awarded Powell an honorary doctorate of science in 1983. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Tohoku_Gakuin_University" title="Tohoku Gakuin University" id="mwARk">Tohoku Gakuin University</a> of Japan honored Powell with a Doctor of Humane Letters in 1986. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Beaver_College" title="Beaver College" class="mw-redirect" id="mwARo">Beaver College</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Berea_College" title="Berea College" id="mwARs">Berea College</a> (his alma mater) have also honored Powell with honorary degrees.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt153" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"AMWS\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwARw"/><sup about="#mwt153" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AMWS_2-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"AMWS"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-AMWS-2" id="mwAR0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAR4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAR8">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASA">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt157" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"BereaDegree\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwASE"/><sup about="#mwt157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BereaDegree_34-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"BereaDegree"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-BereaDegree-34" id="mwASI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASQ">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwASY">The minor planet, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./9739_Powell" title="9739 Powell" class="mw-redirect" id="mwASc">9739 Powell</a>, discovered by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Carolyn_Shoemaker" title="Carolyn Shoemaker" class="mw-redirect" id="mwASg">Carolyn Shoemaker</a>, was named for Powell in 1987.<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt161" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"R","href":"./Template:R"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"\"planet\""}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwASk"/><sup about="#mwt161" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-planet_35-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"planet"},"body":{"html":""}}'><a href="./James_L._Powell#cite_note-planet-35" id="mwASo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASw">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwAS4"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Books">Books</h2>
